{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "```python\ndef is_not_prime(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an integer is a non-prime number.\n    Non-prime numbers include numbers less than 2, and composite numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 2:\n        return True\n    if number == 2:\n        return False\n\n    i = 2\n    while i * i <= number:\n        if number % i == 0:\n            return True\n        i += 1\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef is_not_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the given integer n is a non-prime number.\n    Returns True if n is non-prime, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True  # Numbers less than or equal to 1 are non-prime.\n    if n == 2:\n        return False # 2 is a prime number.\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return True  # Even numbers greater than 2 are non-prime.\n\n    # Check for odd divisors from 3 up to the square root of n.\n    for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return True\n    return False\n```"}
