{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the minimum number of rotations (greater than 0) for a string to return to its original form.\n    Handles empty and single-character strings by returning 1, as rotations must be greater than 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    if n == 0 or n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    temp = s + s\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        rotated_s = temp[i : i + n]\n        if rotated_s == s:\n            return i\n    \n    # Fallback, though for any non-empty string, a rotation equal to its length will always restore it.\n    return n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(text: str, char_to_remove: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes the first and last occurrences of a specified character from a string.\n    If the character appears once, that single occurrence is removed; if zero times, the string is returned unchanged.\"\"\"\n    first_occurrence_index = text.find(char_to_remove)\n    if first_occurrence_index == -1:\n        return text\n\n    # Find the last occurrence by reversing the string and adjusting its index.\n    reversed_text = text[::-1]\n    reversed_char_index = reversed_text.find(char_to_remove)\n    last_occurrence_index = len(text) - 1 - reversed_char_index\n\n    if first_occurrence_index == last_occurrence_index:\n        # Only one occurrence found, remove it.\n        return text[:first_occurrence_index] + text[first_occurrence_index + 1:]\n    else:\n        # Remove the first occurrence.\n        temp_string = text[:first_occurrence_index] + text[first_occurrence_index + 1:]\n        \n        # The index of the last occurrence shifts by -1 due to the removal of the first.\n        adjusted_last_occurrence_index = last_occurrence_index - 1\n\n        # Remove the adjusted last occurrence from the temporary string.\n        return temp_string[:adjusted_last_occurrence_index] + temp_string[adjusted_last_occurrence_index + 1:]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_Occ(input_string: str, char_to_remove: str) -> str:\n    first_idx = input_string.find(char_to_remove)\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        return input_string\n\n    last_idx = input_string.rfind(char_to_remove)\n\n    if first_idx == last_idx:\n        return input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx + 1:]\n    else:\n        temp_string = input_string[:first_idx] + input_string[first_idx + 1:]\n        adjusted_last_idx = last_idx - 1 \n        return temp_string[:adjusted_last_idx] + temp_string[adjusted_last_idx + 1:]\n```"}
