{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef sort_matrix(matrix: List[List[Union[int, float]]]) -> List[List[Union[int, float]]]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a matrix in ascending order based on the sum of its rows.\n    Returns a new matrix with rows reordered, leaving the original unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not matrix:\n        return []\n\n    # Pair each row with its sum for sorting.\n    rows_with_sums = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        rows_with_sums.append((sum(row), row))\n\n    # Sort the pairs based on the calculated row sums.\n    sorted_rows_with_sums = sorted(rows_with_sums, key=lambda item: item[0])\n\n    # Extract and return the sorted rows as a new matrix.\n    return [row for _, row in sorted_rows_with_sums]\n```"}
