{"task_id": "Mbpp/56", "solution": "```python\ndef _reverse_number(num: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses an integer, preserving its sign.\n    Handles positive, negative, and zero inputs efficiently.\n    \"\"\"\n    if num == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    is_negative = num < 0\n    abs_num_str = str(abs(num))\n    reversed_abs_num_str = abs_num_str[::-1]\n    reversed_abs_num = int(reversed_abs_num_str)\n\n    return -reversed_abs_num if is_negative else reversed_abs_num\n\ndef check(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is one less than twice its reverse.\n    This function assumes 'num' is an integer, per critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    reversed_num = _reverse_number(num)\n    return num == (2 * reversed_num) - 1\n```"}
