{"task_id": "Mbpp/57", "solution": "```python\nimport functools\n\ndef compare_digits(a: str, b: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Custom comparison function for sorting digit-strings to form the largest number.\n    It compares concatenations 'b+a' versus 'a+b'.\n    \"\"\"\n    if b + a > a + b:\n        return 1\n    elif b + a < a + b:\n        return -1\n    else:\n        return 0\n\ndef find_Max_Num(digits: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest number that can be formed with the given list of digits.\n    Digits are converted to strings and sorted using a custom comparison logic.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not digits:\n        return 0\n\n    digit_strings = [str(d) for d in digits]\n\n    digit_strings.sort(key=functools.cmp_to_key(compare_digits), reverse=True)\n\n    if digit_strings[0] == '0':\n        return 0\n\n    return int(\"\".join(digit_strings))\n```"}
