{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "```python\ndef count_Substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts substrings where the sum of their digits equals their length.\n    Non-digit characters cause the current substring and longer ones starting at the same point to be skipped.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(s)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_sum = 0\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            try:\n                current_sum += int(s[j])\n            except ValueError:\n                # Non-digit character means this substring and any longer ones\n                # starting with 'i' are invalid, so break and move to next 'i'.\n                break\n\n            substring_length = (j - i) + 1\n\n            if current_sum == substring_length:\n                count += 1\n    return count\n```"}
