{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Bell number using an iterative approach.\n    It uses a nested helper for binomial coefficients and memoization.\"\"\"\n\n    def _binomial_coefficient(n_coeff: int, k_coeff: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates C(n_coeff, k_coeff). Assumes valid inputs as per critical requirements.\"\"\"\n        if k_coeff < 0 or k_coeff > n_coeff:\n            raise ValueError(\"k must be between 0 and n, inclusive.\")\n        if k_coeff == 0 or k_coeff == n_coeff:\n            return 1\n        if k_coeff > n_coeff // 2:\n            k_coeff = n_coeff - k_coeff\n        \n        res = 1\n        for i in range(k_coeff):\n            res = res * (n_coeff - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    \n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    bell_numbers = [0] * (n + 1)\n    bell_numbers[0] = 1 # Initialize B_0\n\n    # Calculate B_1 through B_n using the recurrence relation.\n    for i in range(n): # i iterates from 0 up to n-1 to calculate B_1 up to B_n\n        next_bell = 0\n        for k in range(i + 1):\n            coeff = _binomial_coefficient(i, k)\n            next_bell += coeff * bell_numbers[k]\n        bell_numbers[i + 1] = next_bell\n        \n    return bell_numbers[n]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Monotonic(arr: list) -> bool:\n    if len(arr) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    is_non_decreasing = True\n    is_non_increasing = True\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        if arr[i] < arr[i-1]:\n            is_non_decreasing = False\n        if arr[i] > arr[i-1]:\n            is_non_increasing = False\n\n    return is_non_decreasing or is_non_increasing\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Monotonic(arr):\n    \"\"\"Determines if the input array is monotonic (either increasing or decreasing).\n    Handles empty and single-element arrays correctly.\"\"\"\n\n    if len(arr) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    def _is_increasing(sequence):\n        # Checks if the given sequence is monotonically increasing.\n        for i in range(len(sequence) - 1):\n            if sequence[i] > sequence[i+1]:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def _is_decreasing(sequence):\n        # Checks if the given sequence is monotonically decreasing.\n        for i in range(len(sequence) - 1):\n            if sequence[i] < sequence[i+1]:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    return _is_increasing(arr) or _is_decreasing(arr)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/69", "solution": "```python\ndef is_sublist(main_list: list, sub_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if sub_list is a contiguous sublist of main_list.\n    Returns True if found, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not sub_list:\n        return True\n\n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sub_list)\n\n    if m > n:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if main_list[i:i+m] == sub_list:\n            return True\n    return False\n```"}
