{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "```python\n# Module-level cache for Stirling numbers of the second kind.\\n_stirling_cache = {}\\n\\ndef _stirling_second_kind(n: int, k: int) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Calculates the Stirling number of the second kind S(n, k) using memoization.\\n    This is a helper function used internally by bell_number.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if k < 0 or k > n:\\n        return 0\\n    if n == 0 and k == 0:\\n        return 1\\n    if k == 0 or n == 0: # Catches S(n,0)=0 for n>0 and S(0,k)=0 for k>0\\n        return 0\\n    if k == 1 or k == n:\\n        return 1\\n\\n    if (n, k) in _stirling_cache:\\n        return _stirling_cache[(n, k)]\\n\\n    # Recurrence relation: S(n, k) = k * S(n-1, k) + S(n-1, k-1)\\n    result = k * _stirling_second_kind(n - 1, k) + _stirling_second_kind(n - 1, k - 1)\\n    _stirling_cache[(n, k)] = result\\n    return result\\n\\ndef bell_number(n: int) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Calculates the nth Bell number, which represents the number of ways to partition a set of n elements.\\n    It sums Stirling numbers of the second kind S(n, k) for k from 0 to n.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if n < 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\\\")\\n    if n == 0:\\n        return 1\\n\\n    total_bell = 0\\n    for k in range(n + 1):\\n        total_bell += _stirling_second_kind(n, k)\\n    return total_bell\\n```\"\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "```python\ndef comb_sort(data: list[float | int]) -> list[float | int]:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of numbers using the Comb Sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new sorted list, leaving the original list unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(data)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return list(data)\n\n    arr = list(data)  # Create a mutable copy to perform sorting\n    gap = n\n    shrink_factor = 1.3\n    sorted_flag = False\n\n    while not sorted_flag:\n        gap = int(gap / shrink_factor)\n        if gap <= 1:\n            gap = 1\n            sorted_flag = True  # Assume sorted until a swap occurs\n\n        i = 0\n        while i + gap < n:\n            if arr[i] > arr[i + gap]:\n                arr[i], arr[i + gap] = arr[i + gap], arr[i]\n                sorted_flag = False  # A swap occurred, list is not yet sorted\n            i += 1\n            \n    return arr\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "```python\ndef comb_sort(data):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of elements using the comb sort algorithm.\n    The list is sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(data)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return data[:]\n\n    SHRINK_FACTOR = 1.3\n    gap = n\n    swapped = True\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        if gap > 1:\n            gap = int(gap / SHRINK_FACTOR)\n        \n        swapped = False\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if data[i] > data[i + gap]:\n                data[i], data[i + gap] = data[i + gap], data[i]\n                swapped = True\n    return data[:]\n```"}
