{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "```python\ndef is_samepatterns(words: list[str], patterns: list[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if words follow the pattern, ensuring a consistent one-to-one mapping.\n    Returns True if mapping is consistent, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    if len(words) != len(patterns):\n        return False\n\n    word_to_pattern_map = {}\n    pattern_to_word_map = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(words)):\n        word = words[i]\n        pattern_char = patterns[i]\n\n        # Check word to pattern consistency\n        if word in word_to_pattern_map:\n            if word_to_pattern_map[word] != pattern_char:\n                return False\n        else:\n            word_to_pattern_map[word] = pattern_char\n\n        # Check pattern to word consistency\n        if pattern_char in pattern_to_word_map:\n            if pattern_to_word_map[pattern_char] != word:\n                return False\n        else:\n            pattern_to_word_map[pattern_char] = word\n        \n    return True\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "```python\ndef is_samepatterns(strings: list[str], patterns: list[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list of strings follows a given pattern list.\n    It requires a consistent one-to-one mapping between elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(strings) != len(patterns):\n        return False\n\n    if not strings and not patterns:\n        return True\n\n    string_to_pattern_map = {}\n    pattern_to_string_map = {}\n\n    for s, p in zip(strings, patterns):\n        if s in string_to_pattern_map:\n            if string_to_pattern_map[s] != p:\n                return False\n        else:\n            if p in pattern_to_string_map:\n                return False\n            string_to_pattern_map[s] = p\n            pattern_to_string_map[p] = s\n    return True\n```"}
