{"task_id": "Mbpp/77", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Diff(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if an integer is divisible by 11 using the alternating sum of digits rule.\n    Returns True if the number is divisible by 11, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return True\n\n    # Divisibility by 11 applies to the absolute value of the number.\n    abs_number = abs(number)\n    \n    s = str(abs_number)\n    alternating_sum = 0\n    # Calculate the alternating sum of digits, starting from the rightmost digit.\n    # The rightmost digit (index len(s)-1) is effectively at \"reverse index\" 0.\n    # Digits at even reverse indices get added, odd reverse indices get subtracted.\n    for i, digit_char in enumerate(s):\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        if (len(s) - 1 - i) % 2 == 0:  # Rightmost and every alternate digit from right\n            alternating_sum += digit\n        else:\n            alternating_sum -= digit\n    \n    return alternating_sum % 11 == 0\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "```python\ndef find_tuples(data, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a list of tuples, returning only those where all elements\n    are perfectly divisible by k.\n    \"\"\"\n    filtered_tuples = []\n    for current_tuple in data:\n        all_elements_divisible = True\n        for element in current_tuple:\n            # All inputs are trusted to be valid, including k not being zero.\n            if element % k != 0:\n                all_elements_divisible = False\n                break\n        if all_elements_divisible:\n            filtered_tuples.append(current_tuple)\n    return filtered_tuples\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/77", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Diff(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer is divisible by 11 using the alternating sum of digits rule.\n    The rule applies to the absolute value of the number.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return True\n\n    abs_number_str = str(abs(number))\n    alternating_sum = 0\n    \n    # Iterate from the rightmost digit, alternatingly adding and subtracting.\n    for i, digit_char in enumerate(reversed(abs_number_str)):\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            alternating_sum += digit\n        else:\n            alternating_sum -= digit\n            \n    return alternating_sum % 11 == 0\n```"}
