{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Dict\n\n# Memoization cache for Newman-Conway numbers.\n# Stores previously computed values to optimize recursive calls.\n_memo: Dict[int, int] = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth number of the Newman-Conway sequence.\n    This function uses memoization for efficient computation.\"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    # Apply the Newman-Conway sequence definition recursively.\n    # P(n) = P(P(n - 1)) + P(n - P(n - 1)) for n > 2.\n    pn_minus_1 = sequence(n - 1)\n    ppn_minus_1 = sequence(pn_minus_1)\n    pn_minus_pn_minus_1 = sequence(n - pn_minus_1)\n\n    result = ppn_minus_1 + pn_minus_pn_minus_1\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
