{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "```python\ndef is_undulating(number):\n    s_number = str(abs(number))\n    n = len(s_number)\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # An undulating number must have alternating digits, so the first two cannot be the same.\n    if s_number[0] == s_number[1]:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(2, n):\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # Digits at even indices must match the first digit.\n            if s_number[i] != s_number[0]:\n                return False\n        else:  # Digits at odd indices must match the second digit.\n            if s_number[i] != s_number[1]:\n                return False\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "```python\ndef is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if the input number exhibits an undulating pattern (ABAB...).\n    An undulating number must strictly alternate between two distinct digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_number = str(number)\n\n    # An undulating number must have at least three digits to establish the ABA pattern.\n    if len(s_number) < 3:\n        return False\n\n    first_digit = s_number[0]\n    second_digit = s_number[1]\n\n    # The two alternating digits must be distinct (e.g., 111 is not undulating).\n    if first_digit == second_digit:\n        return False\n\n    # Check if the digits follow the ABABA... pattern.\n    for i in range(len(s_number)):\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # Even-indexed digits should match the first digit.\n            if s_number[i] != first_digit:\n                return False\n        else:  # Odd-indexed digits should match the second digit.\n            if s_number[i] != second_digit:\n                return False\n    return True\n```"}
