{"task_id": "Mbpp/104", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef sort_sublists(data: List[List[str]]) -> List[List[str]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts each sublist of strings in a given list of lists.\n\n    Args:\n        data: A list of lists, where each inner list contains strings.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list of lists with each sublist sorted alphabetically.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input 'data' is not a list, if any element within 'data' is not a list,\n                   or if any element within an inner list is not a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'data' must be a list.\")\n\n    sorted_data = []\n    for i, sublist in enumerate(data):\n        if not isinstance(sublist, list):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Element at index {i} must be a list, got {type(sublist).__name__}.\")\n        \n        for j, item in enumerate(sublist):\n            if not isinstance(item, str):\n                raise TypeError(f\"Element at index [{i}][{j}] must be a string, got {type(item).__name__}.\")\n\n        sorted_data.append(sorted(sublist))\n    return sorted_data\n```"}
