{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(s: str, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts how many rotated forms of a binary string represent an odd decimal number.\n    An odd decimal number has '1' as its least significant (rightmost) bit.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    current_string = s\n\n    for _ in range(n):\n        # A binary number is odd if its last digit is '1'.\n        # This is equivalent to checking if the decimal value is odd.\n        if current_string.endswith('1'):\n            count += 1\n        \n        # Perform one right circular rotation.\n        # Example: \"abc\" -> \"cab\"\n        # If string is empty, it remains empty.\n        if not current_string:\n            break\n        current_string = current_string[-1] + current_string[:-1]\n            \n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "```python\ndef odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, rotations: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts odd decimal equivalents from binary string rotations.\n\n    Args:\n        binary_string: A non-empty string containing only '0' or '1' characters.\n        rotations: A non-negative integer representing the number of rotations.\n\n    Returns:\n        The count of odd decimal equivalents found after performing the rotations.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If binary_string is empty, contains non-binary characters,\n                    or if rotations is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Input validation\n    if not binary_string:\n        raise ValueError(\"Binary string cannot be empty.\")\n    if not all(c in '01' for c in binary_string):\n        raise ValueError(\"Binary string must contain only '0' or '1'.\")\n    if rotations < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Number of rotations cannot be negative.\")\n\n    # Helper function for cyclic right rotation\n    def _rotate_string_right(s: str) -> str:\n        # Since binary_string is validated to be non-empty, s will always be non-empty here.\n        return s[-1] + s[:-1]\n\n    # Helper function to convert binary string to decimal\n    def _binary_to_decimal(binary_str: str) -> int:\n        return int(binary_str, 2)\n\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_binary_string = binary_string\n\n    for _ in range(rotations):\n        decimal_value = _binary_to_decimal(current_binary_string)\n        if decimal_value % 2 != 0:\n            odd_count += 1\n        \n        current_binary_string = _rotate_string_right(current_binary_string)\n\n    return odd_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "```python\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds elements common to all inner lists within a list of lists.\n    Assumes valid input structure and hashable elements as per design.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return []\n\n    # Initialize with the set of elements from the first inner list.\n    common_set = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    # Iterate through the rest of the inner lists and compute intersections.\n    for i in range(1, len(nested_lists)):\n        current_list_set = set(nested_lists[i])\n        common_set = common_set.intersection(current_list_set)\n        if not common_set: # Optimization: if no common elements remain, stop early.\n            break\n\n    return list(common_set)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "```python\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_list: list[list]) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds elements common to all inner lists within a nested list.\n    The order of elements in the returned list is not guaranteed.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_list:\n        return []\n\n    common_elements_set = set(nested_list[0])\n\n    for inner_list in nested_list[1:]:\n        common_elements_set.intersection_update(set(inner_list))\n        if not common_elements_set:\n            return []\n\n    return list(common_elements_set)\n```\n"}
