{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "```python\ndef sum(num1: int, num2: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of common positive divisors for two integers.\n\n    This function finds common divisors by first determining all divisors for each number,\n    then taking their intersection, and finally summing these common divisors.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Find all positive divisors for num1 using an optimized approach up to its square root.\n    divisors1 = set()\n    for i in range(1, int(num1**0.5) + 1):\n        if num1 % i == 0:\n            divisors1.add(i)\n            divisors1.add(num1 // i)\n\n    # Find all positive divisors for num2 using an optimized approach up to its square root.\n    divisors2 = set()\n    for i in range(1, int(num2**0.5) + 1):\n        if num2 % i == 0:\n            divisors2.add(i)\n            divisors2.add(num2 // i)\n\n    # Identify common divisors and compute their sum.\n    common_divisors_sum = 0\n    for divisor in divisors1.intersection(divisors2):\n        common_divisors_sum += divisor\n        \n    return common_divisors_sum\n```"}
