{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "```python\ndef zero_count(numbers: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the ratio of zero elements to non-zero elements in a list of integers.\n    Handles empty arrays and arrays containing only zeroes or only non-zeroes.\n    \"\"\"\n    zeroes = 0\n    non_zeroes = 0\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if num == 0:\n            zeroes += 1\n        else:\n            non_zeroes += 1\n\n    if non_zeroes == 0:\n        return float('inf') if zeroes > 0 else 0.0\n    \n    return float(zeroes) / non_zeroes\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "```python\ndef zero_count(arr: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the ratio of zero elements to non-zero elements in a list of integers.\n    Returns 0.0 if there are no non-zero elements to avoid division by zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_zeroes = 0\n    num_non_zeroes = 0\n\n    for item in arr:\n        if item == 0:\n            num_zeroes += 1\n        else:\n            num_non_zeroes += 1\n\n    if num_non_zeroes == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    else:\n        return float(num_zeroes) / num_non_zeroes\n```"}
