{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks whether the given number can be represented as the sum of non-zero powers of 2.\n    A number can be represented as a sum of non-zero powers of 2 if and only if\n    it is a positive even integer.\n\n    Args:\n        num: The integer to check.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if the number can be represented as a sum of non-zero powers of 2,\n        False otherwise.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If 'num' is not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(num, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'num' must be an integer.\")\n\n    # A number can be represented as a sum of non-zero powers of 2\n    # if it is positive and even.\n    # Examples:\n    # 2 = 2^1\n    # 4 = 2^2\n    # 6 = 2^1 + 2^2\n    # 8 = 2^3\n    # 10 = 2^1 + 2^3\n    # Odd numbers cannot be formed (e.g., 1, 3, 5, 7) because 2^0 (1) is excluded.\n    # Zero and negative numbers are also excluded as sums of positive powers.\n    return num > 0 and num % 2 == 0"}
