{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Any\n\ndef pancake_sort(elements: List[Any]) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of comparable elements using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list with elements in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(elements)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return list(elements)\n\n    working_arr = list(elements)\n\n    def _find_max_index(arr: List[Any], n_current: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the maximum element in the first n_current elements.\"\"\"\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, n_current):\n            if arr[i] > arr[max_idx]:\n                max_idx = i\n        return max_idx\n\n    def _flip(arr: List[Any], i: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Reverses the order of elements from index 0 to i (inclusive).\"\"\"\n        start = 0\n        while start < i:\n            arr[start], arr[i] = arr[i], arr[start]\n            start += 1\n            i -= 1\n\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find index of the maximum element in current sub-array\n        max_idx = _find_max_index(working_arr, current_size)\n\n        # If max element is not already at its correct position\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            # Move the maximum element to the beginning\n            _flip(working_arr, max_idx)\n            # Move the maximum element to its correct position\n            _flip(working_arr, current_size - 1)\n\n    return working_arr\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "```python\ndef pancake_sort(data_list: list[int]) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of integers in-place using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    This function modifies the original list.\"\"\"\n\n    def _find_max_index(arr: list[int], n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the maximum element within the first n elements.\"\"\"\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, n):\n            if arr[i] > arr[max_idx]:\n                max_idx = i\n        return max_idx\n\n    def _flip(arr: list[int], i: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Reverses elements from index 0 to i (inclusive).\"\"\"\n        start = 0\n        while start < i:\n            arr[start], arr[i] = arr[i], arr[start]\n            start += 1\n            i -= 1\n\n    n = len(data_list)\n\n    for current_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current unsorted sublist.\n        max_idx = _find_max_index(data_list, current_size)\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already in its correct position.\n        if max_idx != current_size - 1:\n            # Move the maximum element to the beginning of the list.\n            _flip(data_list, max_idx)\n\n            # Move the maximum element from the beginning to its final sorted position.\n            _flip(data_list, current_size - 1)\n```"}
