{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "```python\ndef find_solution(a: int, b: int, n: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds integer solutions (x, y) for the linear Diophantine equation ax + by = n.\n    Returns (x, y) as a tuple if a solution exists, otherwise None.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _extended_gcd(a_val: int, b_val: int) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Implements the Extended Euclidean Algorithm.\n        Returns (gcd, x, y) such that a_val*x + b_val*y = gcd(a_val, b_val).\n        \"\"\"\n        if a_val == 0:\n            return b_val, 0, 1\n        \n        gcd_val, x1, y1 = _extended_gcd(b_val % a_val, a_val)\n        x = y1 - (b_val // a_val) * x1\n        y = x1\n        return gcd_val, x, y\n\n    # Handle the specific case where both coefficients are zero.\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        return (0, 0) if n == 0 else None\n\n    # Use the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to find gcd(a, b) and a particular solution for gcd.\n    gcd_val, x0, y0 = _extended_gcd(a, b)\n\n    # A solution exists if and only if n is divisible by gcd(a, b).\n    if n % gcd_val != 0:\n        return None\n\n    # Scale the particular solution (x0, y0) to satisfy ax + by = n.\n    k = n // gcd_val\n    x = x0 * k\n    y = y0 * k\n    return x, y\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/160", "solution": "```python\ndef gcd(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the greatest common divisor of two integers using the Euclidean algorithm.\n    Returns the absolute value of the GCD.\n    \"\"\"\n    while b:\n        a, b = b, a % b\n    return abs(a)\n\ndef extended_gcd(a: int, b: int) -> tuple[int, int, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements the Extended Euclidean Algorithm to find g, x, and y such that g = ax + by.\n    g is gcd(a, b).\n    \"\"\"\n    if a == 0:\n        return b, 0, 1\n    g, x, y = extended_gcd(b % a, a)\n    return g, y - (b // a) * x, x\n\ndef find_solution(a: int, b: int, n: int) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Solves the linear Diophantine equation ax + by = n for integers x and y.\n    Returns a particular integer solution (x, y) or None if no solution exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if a == 0 and b == 0:\n        return (0, 0) if n == 0 else None\n\n    if a == 0:\n        if n % b == 0:\n            return (0, n // b)\n        else:\n            return None\n\n    if b == 0:\n        if n % a == 0:\n            return (n // a, 0)\n        else:\n            return None\n\n    g = gcd(a, b)\n    if n % g != 0:\n        return None\n\n    # Solve ax' + by' = g using Extended Euclidean Algorithm\n    g_prime, x_prime, y_prime = extended_gcd(a, b)\n\n    # Scale to find solution for ax + by = n\n    k = n // g\n    x = x_prime * k\n    y = y_prime * k\n\n    return (x, y)\n```"}
