{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "```python\ndef find_even_pair(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts pairs of integers whose bitwise XOR is an even number.\n    This occurs when both integers in a pair have the same parity (both even or both odd).\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(numbers)\n    if n < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    even_count = 0\n    odd_count = 0\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            even_count += 1\n        else:\n            odd_count += 1\n\n    # Calculate combinations of (even, even) pairs and (odd, odd) pairs.\n    even_even_pairs = (even_count * (even_count - 1)) // 2\n    odd_odd_pairs = (odd_count * (odd_count - 1)) // 2\n\n    return even_even_pairs + odd_odd_pairs\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "```python\ndef find_even_pair(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts pairs whose XOR sum is even (i.e., numbers have the same parity).\n    Iterates through all unique pairs and increments a counter if parities match.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(numbers)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            # The XOR sum (a ^ b) is even if and only if 'a' and 'b' have the same parity.\n            if (numbers[i] % 2) == (numbers[j] % 2):\n                count += 1\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/167", "solution": "```python\ndef next_power_of_2(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the smallest power of 2 greater than or equal to n.\n    This function uses bitwise operations for O(1) performance.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n    if (n & (n - 1)) == 0:  # Check if n is already a power of 2\n        return n\n    \n    # Use bit manipulation to find the next power of 2.\n    # Decrement n, then fill all bits to the right of the MSB with ones.\n    n -= 1\n    n |= n >> 1\n    n |= n >> 2\n    n |= n >> 4\n    n |= n >> 8\n    n |= n >> 16\n    n |= n >> 32\n    return n + 1\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/167", "solution": "```python\ndef next_power_of_2(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the smallest power of 2 greater than or equal to n.\n    This function trusts that n is a non-negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return 1\n\n    power = 1\n    while power < n:\n        power *= 2\n    return power\n```"}
