{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "```python\nimport collections\n\ndef check_occurences(tuple_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts occurrences of tuples, treating tuples with the same elements (regardless of order) as equivalent.\n    Returns a dictionary mapping normalized tuples to their counts.\n    \"\"\"\n    occurrences = collections.defaultdict(int)\n    for item_tuple in tuple_list:\n        normalized_key = tuple(sorted(item_tuple))\n        occurrences[normalized_key] += 1\n    return dict(occurrences)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "```python\ndef check_occurences(list_of_tuples: list[tuple]) -> dict[tuple, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts occurrences of tuples, treating (a, b) and (b, a) as identical.\n    Returns a dictionary mapping canonical tuples to their counts.\n    \"\"\"\n    occurrences = {}\n    for t in list_of_tuples:\n        # Normalize the tuple by sorting its elements to create a canonical form.\n        canonical_t = tuple(sorted(t))\n        occurrences[canonical_t] = occurrences.get(canonical_t, 0) + 1\n    return occurrences\n```"}
