{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "```python\ndef even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all bits at odd positions (1, 3, 5, ...) to 1 in the given number.\n    The function uses a bitwise OR operation with a suitable mask.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        # For simplicity, we'll assume non-negative or handle as if unsigned.\n        pass\n\n    if number == 0:\n        return 0\n        \n    max_bit_length = number.bit_length()\n    mask = 0\n\n    for i in range(1, max_bit_length + 1, 2):\n        mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    return number | mask\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "```python\nfrom functools import lru_cache\n\ndef get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the total number of sequences of length n.\n    Each element x_i in a sequence must satisfy 1 <= x_i <= m and x_i >= 2 * x_{i-1}.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n\n    @lru_cache(None)\n    def _calculate_sequences_recursive(current_val: int, length_remaining: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Helper function to recursively count valid sequences with memoization.\"\"\"\n        if length_remaining == 0:\n            return 1 # A valid sequence of the desired length has been formed\n\n        count = 0\n        min_next_val = current_val * 2\n        for next_val in range(min_next_val, m + 1):\n            count += _calculate_sequences_recursive(next_val, length_remaining - 1)\n        return count\n\n    total_sequences = 0\n    # The first element can be any value from 1 to m\n    for first_val in range(1, m + 1):\n        total_sequences += _calculate_sequences_recursive(first_val, n - 1)\n    \n    return total_sequences\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "```python\ndef get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of sequences of length n with elements up to m,\n    where each element is at least twice the previous one.\n    \"\"\"\n    dp = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: sequences of length 1. Any positive integer up to m is valid.\n    for j in range(1, m + 1):\n        dp[1][j] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for lengths from 2 to n.\n    for i in range(2, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, m + 1):  # current element\n            # Sum up counts from sequences of length i-1 ending with k, where 2*k <= j.\n            for k in range(1, m + 1):  # previous element\n                if 2 * k <= j:\n                    dp[i][j] += dp[i-1][k]\n                else:\n                    # Optimization: as k increases, 2*k will only get larger, so we can break.\n                    break\n    \n    # The total number of sequences of length n is the sum of all possibilities for the last element.\n    total_sequences = sum(dp[n][j] for j in range(1, m + 1))\n    return total_sequences\n```"}
