{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "def maximize_elements(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Maximizes corresponding elements within two tuples of tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple1: The first input tuple of tuples.\n        tuple2: The second input tuple of tuples.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new tuple of tuples with maximized elements.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If inputs are not tuples, or if inner elements are not tuples.\n        ValueError: If outer tuple lengths or corresponding inner tuple lengths do not match.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(tuple2, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both inputs must be tuples.\")\n\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same number of inner tuples.\")\n\n    maximized_outer_tuple = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        inner_tuple1 = tuple1[i]\n        inner_tuple2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        if not isinstance(inner_tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(inner_tuple2, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Inner elements at index {i} must be tuples.\")\n\n        if len(inner_tuple1) != len(inner_tuple2):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Inner tuples at index {i} must have the same number of elements.\")\n\n        maximized_inner_tuple = []\n        for j in range(len(inner_tuple1)):\n            maximized_inner_tuple.append(max(inner_tuple1[j], inner_tuple2[j]))\n        maximized_outer_tuple.append(tuple(maximized_inner_tuple))\n\n    return tuple(maximized_outer_tuple)"}
