{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "```python\ndef list_split(input_list: list, n: int) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits a list into n sublists by distributing elements cyclically.\n    Elements are distributed such that an item at index `i` goes to sublist `i % n`.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: The original list to be split.\n        n: The number of sublists to create.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list containing n sublists.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is less than or equal to 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    result = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    for index, item in enumerate(input_list):\n        target_sublist_index = index % n\n        result[target_sublist_index].append(item)\n\n    return result\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "def list_split(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Splits a list into n sublists based on an nth element distribution.\n    Each sublist contains elements from the original list at intervals of n.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The design specification's error handling for 'n' has been omitted\n    # per critical requirements, trusting the caller's input.\n\n    # Handle empty input list gracefully (FR2)\n    if not input_list:\n        return [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Initialize n empty sublists\n    result = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Distribute elements to sublists based on modulo n (FR1)\n    for i, item in enumerate(input_list):\n        result[i % n].append(item)\n    \n    return result"}
