{"task_id": "Mbpp/282", "solution": "```python\nclass ListLengthMismatchError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception raised when two lists have different lengths for an element-wise operation.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Input lists must have the same length.\"):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\ndef sub_list(list1: list, list2: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Subtracts two lists element-wise.\n\n    Args:\n        list1: The first list of numbers.\n        list2: The second list of numbers to subtract from the first.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list with the element-wise differences.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If inputs are not lists or contain non-numeric elements.\n        ListLengthMismatchError: If the input lists have different lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(list1, list) or not isinstance(list2, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Both inputs must be lists.\")\n    if len(list1) != len(list2):\n        raise ListLengthMismatchError(\"Input lists must have the same length for element-wise subtraction.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(list1)):\n        if not isinstance(list1[i], (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Element at index {i} in the first list is not numeric.\")\n        if not isinstance(list2[i], (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Element at index {i} in the second list is not numeric.\")\n        result.append(list1[i] - list2[i])\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "```python\ndef validate(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    Handles negative numbers by using their absolute value and treats '0' as a special case.\n    \"\"\"\n    num_str = str(abs(number))\n    digit_counts = {}\n    for char_digit in num_str:\n        digit_counts[char_digit] = digit_counts.get(char_digit, 0) + 1\n\n    for digit_char, frequency in digit_counts.items():\n        digit_value = int(digit_char)\n        if digit_value == 0:\n            return False\n        if frequency > digit_value:\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
