{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef validate(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n\n    Args:\n        number: The integer to validate.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if the frequency of each digit is <= the digit's value, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(number, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n    \n    if number < 0:\n        # Handle negative numbers by validating their absolute value\n        number = abs(number)\n    \n    if number == 0:\n        # Special case: digit 0 appears once. Frequency (1) > digit value (0).\n        # This condition (1 <= 0) is false, so it should return False.\n        return False\n\n    s_number = str(number)\n    digit_counts = Counter(s_number)\n\n    for digit_char, frequency in digit_counts.items():\n        digit_value = int(digit_char)\n        # If digit is 0, its value is 0. Any frequency > 0 will fail as frequency cannot be <= 0.\n        # Since it appeared, frequency must be >= 1. So it always fails.\n        if digit_value == 0:\n            return False\n        if frequency > digit_value:\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
