{"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "```python\ndef _merge_and_count(left: list, right: list) -> tuple[int, list]:\n    \"\"\"Merges two sorted arrays and counts inversions between them.\n    Returns the count of inversions and the merged sorted array.\"\"\"\n    merged = []\n    i, j = 0, 0\n    inversions = 0\n\n    while i < len(left) and j < len(right):\n        if left[i] <= right[j]:\n            merged.append(left[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            merged.append(right[j])\n            inversions += (len(left) - i)\n            j += 1\n\n    merged.extend(left[i:])\n    merged.extend(right[j:])\n\n    return inversions, merged\n\ndef _merge_sort_and_count(arr: list) -> tuple[int, list]:\n    \"\"\"Recursively sorts the array and counts inversions.\n    Returns the total inversions and the sorted array.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n < 2:\n        return 0, arr\n\n    mid = n // 2\n    left_inversions, left_half = _merge_sort_and_count(arr[:mid])\n    right_inversions, right_half = _merge_sort_and_count(arr[mid:])\n\n    merged_inversions, merged_array = _merge_and_count(left_half, right_half)\n\n    return left_inversions + right_inversions + merged_inversions, merged_array\n\ndef get_Inv_Count(arr: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts inversions in an array using a modified merge sort.\n    An inversion is a pair of indices (i, j) such that i < j and arr[i] > arr[j].\"\"\"\n    if len(arr) < 2:\n        return 0\n\n    inversions, _ = _merge_sort_and_count(arr)\n    return inversions\n```"}
