{"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "```python\ndef get_Inv_Count(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of inversions in an array using a modified merge sort.\n    An inversion is a pair (i, j) such that i < j and arr[i] > arr[j].\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _merge_sort_and_count(current_arr):\n        \"\"\"Recursively sorts the array and counts inversions.\"\"\"\n        n = len(current_arr)\n        if n <= 1:\n            return current_arr, 0\n\n        mid = n // 2\n        left_half, left_inversions = _merge_sort_and_count(current_arr[:mid])\n        right_half, right_inversions = _merge_sort_and_count(current_arr[mid:])\n\n        merged_array, split_inversions = _merge_and_count_split_inv(left_half, right_half)\n\n        total_inversions = left_inversions + right_inversions + split_inversions\n        return merged_array, total_inversions\n\n    def _merge_and_count_split_inv(left, right):\n        \"\"\"Merges two sorted arrays and counts inversions between them.\"\"\"\n        merged = []\n        i, j = 0, 0\n        split_inversions = 0\n        len_left = len(left)\n\n        while i < len(left) and j < len(right):\n            if left[i] <= right[j]:\n                merged.append(left[i])\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                merged.append(right[j])\n                split_inversions += (len_left - i)\n                j += 1\n\n        merged.extend(left[i:])\n        merged.extend(right[j:])\n        return merged, split_inversions\n\n    _, count = _merge_sort_and_count(arr)\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/297", "solution": "```python\ndef flatten_list(nested_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Flattens a given nested list structure into a single-level list.\n    Returns a new list containing all elements from the input list and its sub-lists, in order.\n    \"\"\"\n    flat_list = []\n    for item in nested_list:\n        if isinstance(item, list):\n            flat_list.extend(flatten_list(item))\n        else:\n            flat_list.append(item)\n    return flat_list\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "```python\ndef max_aggregate(data: list[tuple[str, int]]) -> tuple[str, int] | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum aggregated score from a list of (name, score) tuples.\n    Aggregates scores for each name and returns the name with the highest total score.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        return None\n\n    aggregated_scores = {}\n    for name, score in data:\n        aggregated_scores[name] = aggregated_scores.get(name, 0) + score\n\n    max_name = None\n    max_score = -1  # Scores are non-negative, so -1 is a safe initial minimum\n\n    for name, score in aggregated_scores.items():\n        if score > max_score:\n            max_score = score\n            max_name = name\n\n    return (max_name, max_score)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "```python\ndef max_aggregate(data: list[tuple[str, int]]) -> tuple[str, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum aggregate score from a list of (name, score) tuples.\n    Returns the name and total score of the individual with the highest aggregate score.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        return (\"\", 0)\n\n    aggregate_scores = {}\n    for name, score in data:\n        if name in aggregate_scores:\n            aggregate_scores[name] += score\n        else:\n            aggregate_scores[name] = score\n\n    max_name = \"\"\n    max_score = -float('inf')\n\n    for name, score in aggregate_scores.items():\n        if score > max_score:\n            max_score = score\n            max_name = name\n\n    return (max_name, max_score)\n```"}
