{"task_id": "Mbpp/301", "solution": "```python\ndef dict_depth(data):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum nesting depth of a dictionary.\n    Returns 0 if the input is not a dictionary, otherwise the depth starts at 1.\"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_depth_recursive(current_dict, current_level):\n        max_depth_in_branch = current_level\n        for value in current_dict.values():\n            if isinstance(value, dict):\n                nested_depth = _calculate_depth_recursive(value, current_level + 1)\n                max_depth_in_branch = max(max_depth_in_branch, nested_depth)\n        return max_depth_in_branch\n\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        return 0\n\n    return _calculate_depth_recursive(data, 1)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/301", "solution": "```python\ndef dict_depth(data: dict) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum nesting depth of a dictionary.\n    The depth is 1 for a flat dictionary and increments for each nested level.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_depth = 1\n    for value in data.values():\n        if isinstance(value, dict):\n            max_depth = max(max_depth, 1 + dict_depth(value))\n    return max_depth\n```"}
