m.\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if arr[k] > arr[j]:\n            overall_max_sum = max(overall_max_sum, dp_prefix_sums[j] + arr[k])\n    \n    return overall_max_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "```python\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(arr: list[int], n: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from arr[0...i]\n    that includes arr[k], where prefix elements are less than arr[k].\n    Assumes valid inputs as per problem specifications.\n    \"\"\"\n    # dp[j] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at index j\n    # within arr[0...i], such that arr[j] < arr[k].\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n    max_prefix_sum_ending_before_k = 0\n\n    for current_idx in range(i + 1):\n        current_val = arr[current_idx]\n        # Only consider elements from prefix that are less than arr[k]\n        if current_val < arr[k]:\n            # Subsequence ending at current_idx can be just current_val\n            dp[current_idx] = current_val\n            for prev_idx in range(current_idx):\n                # If a previous element can extend the increasing subsequence\n                if arr[prev_idx] < current_val:\n                    dp[current_idx] = max(dp[current_idx], dp[prev_idx] + current_val)\n            # Update the maximum sum found among valid prefix subsequences\n            max_prefix_sum_ending_before_k = max(max_prefix_sum_ending_before_k, dp[current_idx])\n\n    return max_prefix_sum_ending_before_k + arr[k]\n```"}
