{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the leftmost (most significant) unset bit in a non-negative integer.\n    Finds the first zero bit from the most significant bit position upwards and sets it.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Determine the position of the most significant bit (MSB) currently set in n.\n    msb_pos = n.bit_length() - 1\n\n    # Iterate from msb_pos upwards to find the first unset bit.\n    p = msb_pos\n    while True:\n        if not ((n >> p) & 1):  # Check if the bit at position p is 0.\n            return n | (1 << p)  # Set the bit and return.\n        p += 1\n```"}
