{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the left-most unset bit in the given integer.\n    This identifies the most significant 0-bit and sets it to 1.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    if n >= 0:\n        # For positive numbers, search for the most significant 0-bit within its current bit representation.\n        # Iterate from the highest set bit position (n.bit_length() - 1) downwards.\n        highest_set_bit_pos = n.bit_length() - 1\n        for i in range(highest_set_bit_pos, -1, -1):\n            if not ((n >> i) & 1):  # If the i-th bit is 0\n                return n | (1 << i)\n        # If all bits from highest_set_bit_pos down to 0 are set (e.g., n=7, 0b111).\n        # The left-most unset bit is the next higher bit, at n.bit_length().\n        return n | (1 << n.bit_length())\n    else:  # n < 0\n        # For negative numbers, find the most significant 0-bit in its two's complement.\n        # Python's arbitrary precision requires searching up to a practical limit.\n        DEFAULT_SEARCH_BITS_FOR_NEGATIVE = 128\n        search_range_limit = abs(n).bit_length() + DEFAULT_SEARCH_BITS_FOR_NEGATIVE\n        for i in range(search_range_limit, -1, -1):\n            if not ((n >> i) & 1):  # If the i-th bit is 0\n                return n | (1 << i)\n        # If all bits within the search range are set (e.g., n = -1), return original n.\n        return n\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/312", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef volume_cone(radius: float, height: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the volume of a right circular cone.\n\n    Args:\n        radius: The radius of the cone's base. Must be a positive number.\n        height: The height of the cone. Must be a positive number.\n\n    Returns:\n        The calculated volume of the cone as a float.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If radius or height are not positive numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(radius, (int, float)) or radius <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Radius must be a positive number.\")\n    if not isinstance(height, (int, float)) or height <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Height must be a positive number.\")\n\n    return (1/3) * math.pi * (radius ** 2) * height\n```"}
