{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "```python\n# Initialize the memoization cache globally to persist across function calls.\\n_memoization_cache = {}\\n\\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Calculates the maximum sum for \\'n\\' using a recursive formula with memoization.\\n    The formula used is f(n) = max( (f(n//2) + f(n//3) + f(n//4) + f(n//5)), n).\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if n == 0:\\n        return 0\\n\\n    if n in _memoization_cache:\\n        return _memoization_cache[n]\\n\\n    # Calculate sum of parts using integer division for recursive calls.\\n    sum_of_parts = (\\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\\n    )\\n\\n    result = max(sum_of_parts, n)\\n    _memoization_cache[n] = result\\n    return result\\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "def get_max_sum(n: int, _cache: dict = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum for a non-negative integer n using a recursive formula with memoization.\n    The function trusts that input 'n' will be a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n    if _cache is None:\n        _cache = {}\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n in _cache:\n        return _cache[n]\n\n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2, _cache) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3, _cache) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4, _cache) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5, _cache)\n    )\n    \n    result = max(sum_of_parts, n)\n    _cache[n] = result\n    return result"}
