{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_of_digits(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the total sum of digits for all numbers in a given list.\n    Assumes all input numbers are non-negative integers.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_single_number_sum(number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of digits for a single non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n        s = 0\n        num_str = str(number)\n        for digit_char in num_str:\n            s += int(digit_char)\n        return s\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for num in numbers:\n        total_sum += _calculate_single_number_sum(num)\n    return total_sum\n```"}
