{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef min_product_tuple(data: list[tuple]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum product from the pairs of tuples within a given list.\n\n    Args:\n        data: A list of tuples. Each tuple should contain numeric elements.\n\n    Returns:\n        The minimum product found among all tuples.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If data is not a list or if any item in data is not a tuple.\n        ValueError: If data is an empty list, or if any tuple contains non-numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'data' must be a list.\")\n    if not data:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list 'data' cannot be empty.\")\n\n    min_prod = math.inf\n\n    for item in data:\n        if not isinstance(item, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(\"Each item in the list must be a tuple.\")\n\n        current_prod = 1\n        if not item:  # Product of an empty tuple is 1 (multiplicative identity)\n            current_prod = 1\n        else:\n            for element in item:\n                if not isinstance(element, (int, float)):\n                    raise ValueError(f\"Tuple elements must be numeric (int or float), got {type(element).__name__}.\")\n                current_prod *= element\n        \n        if current_prod < min_prod:\n            min_prod = current_prod\n    \n    return min_prod\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/409", "solution": "```python\ndef min_product_tuple(tuple_list: list[tuple[int | float, int | float]]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the product of elements for each tuple and returns the minimum.\n    Assumes valid input structure as per critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    products = []\n    for tpl in tuple_list:\n        product = tpl[0] * tpl[1]\n        products.append(product)\n    return min(products)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/410", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\ndef min_val(data_list: List[Union[str, int, float]]) -> Union[int, float, None]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum numerical value in a heterogeneous list, ignoring non-numerical elements.\n    Returns None if no numerical values are present.\n    \"\"\"\n    numerical_values = []\n    for item in data_list:\n        if isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            numerical_values.append(item)\n\n    if not numerical_values:\n        return None\n    \n    return min(numerical_values)\n```"}
