{"task_id": "Mbpp/413", "solution": "```python\ndef extract_nth_element(data: list[tuple], n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts the element at index 'n' from each tuple within the input 'data' list.\n\n    Args:\n        data: A list where each element is expected to be a tuple.\n        n: The 0-based index of the element to extract from each tuple.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list containing the extracted elements.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If 'data' is not a list or 'n' is not an integer,\n                   or if any element in 'data' is not a tuple.\n        IndexError: If 'n' is out of bounds for any tuple in 'data'.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'data' must be a list.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n\n    extracted_elements = []\n    for item_tuple in data:\n        if not isinstance(item_tuple, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(f\"All elements in 'data' must be tuples, but found: {type(item_tuple)}\")\n        extracted_elements.append(item_tuple[n])\n    return extracted_elements\n```"}
