{"task_id": "Mbpp/420", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"\n    Exception raised for invalid input.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef cube_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the cube sum of the first n even natural numbers.\n\n    Args:\n        n (int): The number of even natural numbers to consider.\n                 Must be a positive integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The calculated cube sum.\n\n    Raises:\n        InvalidInputError: If n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        even_number = 2 * i\n        total_sum += even_number ** 3\n    return total_sum\n```"}
