{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "```python\nimport re\nimport string\nfrom typing import Optional, Tuple\n\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence: str) -> Optional[Tuple[int, int, str]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first adverb in a sentence and returns its position and the cleaned adverb string.\n    Adverbs are primarily identified by ending in 'ly', excluding specific adjectives.\n    \"\"\"\n    ADJECTIVE_EXCLUSION_LIST = [\n        \"friendly\", \"lovely\", \"ugly\", \"lonely\", \"silly\", \"holy\", \"daily\", \"early\",\n        \"elderly\", \"ghastly\", \"jolly\", \"lively\", \"manly\", \"masterly\", \"meekly\",\n        \"oily\", \"only\", \"orderly\", \"saintly\", \"scholarly\", \"shapely\", \"sisterly\",\n        \"stately\", \"timely\", \"unruly\", \"weekly\", \"worldly\", \"yearly\"\n    ]\n\n    # Helper function to clean a word by stripping leading/trailing punctuation.\n    def _clean_word(word: str) -> str:\n        return word.strip(string.punctuation)\n\n    # Helper function to check if a cleaned word is an adverb based on heuristics.\n    def _is_adverb(cleaned_word: str) -> bool:\n        lower_word = cleaned_word.lower()\n        return lower_word.endswith(\"ly\") and lower_word not in ADJECTIVE_EXCLUSION_LIST\n\n    # Input validation as per design\n    if not isinstance(sentence, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'sentence' must be a string.\")\n\n    # Iterate through the sentence using regex to find words and their exact spans,\n    # including any attached punctuation.\n    for match in re.finditer(r'\\b\\w+\\b|\\S+', sentence):\n        word_with_punctuation = match.group(0)\n        original_start_index = match.start()\n\n        cleaned_word = _clean_word(word_with_punctuation)\n\n        # Check if the cleaned word is an adverb and is not empty.\n        if cleaned_word and _is_adverb(cleaned_word):\n            # Calculate the end index for the cleaned adverb string within the original sentence.\n            # This matches the user's assert example (0, 7, 'clearly') for 'clearly!!'\n            end_index = original_start_index + len(cleaned_word)\n            return (original_start_index, end_index, cleaned_word)\n    \n    # If no adverb is found after checking all words, return None.\n    return None\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "```python\nimport re\nimport string\nfrom typing import Optional, Tuple, Set\n\nCOMMON_ADVERBS: Set[str] = {\"very\", \"always\", \"never\", \"well\", \"fast\", \"hard\", \"late\", \"early\", \"soon\", \"often\", \"just\", \"still\", \"already\", \"yet\"}\n\ndef clean_word(word: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes leading and trailing punctuation from a word.\n    \"\"\"\n    return word.strip(string.punctuation)\n\ndef is_adverb(word: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a cleaned word is an adverb based on heuristics.\n    Checks for 'ly' suffix or presence in common adverbs list.\n    \"\"\"\n    lower_word = word.lower()\n    if lower_word in COMMON_ADVERBS:\n        return True\n    if lower_word.endswith(\"ly\") and len(lower_word) > 2:\n        return True\n    return False\n\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence: str) -> Optional[Tuple[int, int, str]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first adverb and its positions in a given sentence.\n    Returns the cleaned adverb string and its start/end indices in the original sentence.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_start_idx = float('inf')\n    result: Optional[Tuple[int, int, str]] = None\n\n    for match in re.finditer(r'\\S+', sentence):\n        word_with_punctuation = match.group(0)\n        original_span_start = match.start()\n\n        cleaned_word = clean_word(word_with_punctuation)\n\n        if cleaned_word and is_adverb(cleaned_word):\n            # Calculate the precise start and end indices of the cleaned word\n            # within its original span in the sentence.\n            # We need to find where the cleaned_word starts within the word_with_punctuation\n            # to adjust the starting index correctly.\n            # Example: \"clearly!!\" -> \"clearly\". The relative start of \"clearly\" in \"clearly!!\" is 0.\n            # Example: \"  quickly,  \" -> \"quickly\". The relative start of \"quickly\" in \"  quickly,  \" needs to be handled\n            # by clean_word already removing leading/trailing punctuation.\n            # If the clean_word results from stripping punctuation, its start relative\n            # to word_with_punctuation is often 0 or the first non-punctuation character.\n            # The most robust way to find the actual start of the *cleaned* word\n            # is to find its first occurrence in the original word_with_punctuation string.\n            # This accounts for cases like '!!clearly!!'\n            \n            # Since clean_word only strips leading/trailing punctuation,\n            # the cleaned_word will always be a substring of word_with_punctuation.\n            # The .find() method will give us the starting index of the cleaned_word\n            # within the word_with_punctuation string.\n            cleaned_word_relative_start = word_with_punctuation.find(cleaned_word)\n            \n            actual_start_idx = original_span_start + cleaned_word_relative_start\n            actual_end_idx = actual_start_idx + len(cleaned_word)\n            \n            if actual_start_idx < min_start_idx:\n                min_start_idx = actual_start_idx\n                result = (actual_start_idx, actual_end_idx, cleaned_word)\n    \n    return result\n```"}
