{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "def index_multiplication(\n    tuple1: tuple[tuple[int | float, ...], ...],\n    tuple2: tuple[tuple[int | float, ...], ...]\n) -> tuple[tuple[int | float, ...], ...]:\n    \"\"\"Performs element-wise multiplication of two nested tuples.\"\"\"\n    \n    result_outer_tuple = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        inner_tuple1 = tuple1[i]\n        inner_tuple2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        result_inner_tuple = []\n        for j in range(len(inner_tuple1)):\n            val1 = inner_tuple1[j]\n            val2 = inner_tuple2[j]\n            \n            result_inner_tuple.append(val1 * val2)\n        result_outer_tuple.append(tuple(result_inner_tuple))\n    \n    return tuple(result_outer_tuple)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "```python\ndef index_multiplication(\n    tuple1: tuple[tuple[int | float, ...], ...],\n    tuple2: tuple[tuple[int | float, ...], ...]\n) -> tuple[tuple[int | float, ...], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs element-wise multiplication of two nested tuple structures.\n    Assumes inputs are valid tuples of tuples with numeric elements and matching structure.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_outer_list = []\n    # Iterate through the outer tuples simultaneously.\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        result_inner_list = []\n        # Iterate through the elements of the inner tuples simultaneously.\n        for j in range(len(tuple1[i])):\n            product = tuple1[i][j] * tuple2[i][j]\n            result_inner_list.append(product)\n        result_outer_list.append(tuple(result_inner_list))\n\n    return tuple(result_outer_list)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/446", "solution": "```python\ndef count_Occurrence(data_tuple: tuple, elements_to_count: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts total occurrences of elements from a list within a tuple.\n    For efficiency, the list of elements to count is converted to a set for O(1) average-case lookup.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    elements_set = set(elements_to_count)\n\n    for item in data_tuple:\n        if item in elements_set:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/446", "solution": "```python\ndef count_Occurrence(input_tuple, input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the total occurrences of elements from input_list within input_tuple.\n    Returns the sum of counts for all specified list elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    tuple_counts = {}\n    for element in input_tuple:\n        tuple_counts[element] = tuple_counts.get(element, 0) + 1\n\n    total_count = 0\n    for item in input_list:\n        total_count += tuple_counts.get(item, 0)\n\n    return total_count\n```"}
