{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "```python\n# The memoization cache for Perrin numbers.\n# P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2 are base cases.\n_perrin_cache = {\n    0: 3,\n    1: 0,\n    2: 2\n}\n\ndef _get_perrin_number(k):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the k-th Perrin number using memoization.\n\n    Args:\n        k: The index of the Perrin number to calculate.\n\n    Returns:\n        The k-th Perrin number.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If k is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Perrin number index cannot be negative.\")\n    if k in _perrin_cache:\n        return _perrin_cache[k]\n    \n    # Calculate recursively and store in cache.\n    p_k = _get_perrin_number(k - 2) + _get_perrin_number(k - 3)\n    _perrin_cache[k] = p_k\n    return p_k\n\ndef cal_sum(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n).\n\n    Args:\n        n: The upper limit (inclusive) for the Perrin number index.\n\n    Returns:\n        The sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n).\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' for sum of Perrin numbers cannot be negative.\")\n        \n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        total_sum += _get_perrin_number(i)\n    return total_sum\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "The function `cal_sum` calculates the sum of Perrin numbers up to a given non-negative integer `n`.\n\nIt handles invalid input by raising an `InvalidInputError` if `n` is negative or not an integer. The Perrin numbers are defined as P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2, and P(k) = P(k-2) + P(k-3) for k > 2.\n\n```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input parameters.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n).\n    Raises InvalidInputError if n is negative or not an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 3\n\n    # Initialize for P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2\n    # p_k_minus_3, p_k_minus_2, p_k_minus_1 track P(i-3), P(i-2), P(i-1) respectively.\n    p_k_minus_3 = 3\n    p_k_minus_2 = 0\n    p_k_minus_1 = 2\n\n    if n == 1:\n        return p_k_minus_3 + p_k_minus_2  # Sum P(0) + P(1) = 3 + 0 = 3\n\n    current_sum = p_k_minus_3 + p_k_minus_2 + p_k_minus_1 # Sum for P(0), P(1), P(2) = 5\n\n    # Calculate remaining Perrin numbers and add to sum\n    for _ in range(3, n + 1):\n        next_perrin = p_k_minus_3 + p_k_minus_2\n        current_sum += next_perrin\n\n        # Shift values for the next iteration: P(i-3) becomes P(i-2), etc.\n        p_k_minus_3 = p_k_minus_2\n        p_k_minus_2 = p_k_minus_1\n        p_k_minus_1 = next_perrin\n\n    return current_sum\n```\n"}
