{"task_id": "Mbpp/453", "solution": "```python\ndef sumofFactors(number):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all even factors for a given number.\n    Assumes the input is a positive integer, as per requirements.\"\"\"\n    sum_of_even_factors = 0\n    for i in range(1, int(number**0.5) + 1):\n        if number % i == 0:\n            factor1 = i\n            factor2 = number // i\n\n            if factor1 % 2 == 0:\n                sum_of_even_factors += factor1\n            \n            if factor1 != factor2:\n                if factor2 % 2 == 0:\n                    sum_of_even_factors += factor2\n    return sum_of_even_factors\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/453", "solution": "```python\ndef sumofFactors(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all positive even factors of a given integer n.\n\n    Args:\n        n: The integer for which to find the sum of even factors.\n\n    Returns:\n        The sum of positive even factors of n.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If n is not an integer.\n        ValueError: If n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Iterate up to sqrt(n) to find factors efficiently\n    for i in range(1, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            factor1 = i\n            factor2 = n // i\n\n            # Check factor1\n            if factor1 % 2 == 0:\n                total_sum += factor1\n\n            # Check factor2, but only if it's different from factor1\n            if factor1 != factor2 and factor2 % 2 == 0:\n                total_sum += factor2\n    return total_sum\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/454", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\n# Compile the regex pattern once for efficiency.\n# It matches a word boundary, zero or more word characters, 'z', more word characters, then a boundary.\n_Z_WORD_PATTERN = re.compile(r'\\b\\w*z\\w*\\b')\n\ndef text_match_wordz(text: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given text contains any word with the letter 'z' (case-sensitive).\n    Assumes valid string input as per requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    return bool(_Z_WORD_PATTERN.search(text))\n```"}
