{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "```python\ndef Find_Min(list_of_lists: list[list]) -> list | None:\n    \"\"\"Finds the sublist with the minimum length from a list of lists.\n    Returns the first encountered sublist if multiple share the minimum length, or None if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_length = float('inf')\n    min_sublist = None\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        if len(sublist) < min_length:\n            min_length = len(sublist)\n            min_sublist = sublist\n\n    return min_sublist\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/457", "solution": "```python\ndef Find_Min(list_of_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds and returns the sublist with the minimum length from a list of lists.\n\n    Args:\n        list_of_lists: A list where each element is itself a list.\n\n    Returns:\n        The sublist with the minimum length. If multiple sublists have the\n        same minimum length, the first one encountered is returned.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input list_of_lists is empty.\n        TypeError: If list_of_lists is not a list, or if any of its elements\n                   are not lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(list_of_lists, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if not list_of_lists:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list_of_lists cannot be empty.\")\n\n    min_sublist = None\n    min_length = float('inf')\n\n    for sublist in list_of_lists:\n        if not isinstance(sublist, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"All elements in list_of_lists must be lists.\")\n\n        if len(sublist) < min_length:\n            min_length = len(sublist)\n            min_sublist = sublist\n    \n    # This case should ideally not be reached if list_of_lists is not empty\n    # and contains only lists, as min_sublist would be initialized.\n    # However, for robustness, we ensure it's not None.\n    if min_sublist is None:\n        # This implies an empty list_of_lists was somehow passed after initial check,\n        # or a very unusual scenario.\n        raise ValueError(\"Could not determine minimum length sublist.\")\n\n    return min_sublist\n```"}
