{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "```python\nimport itertools\n\ndef combinations_list(input_list: list) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all possible combinations of the elements of a given list.\n\n    This function generates combinations by iteratively adding each element\n    from the input_list to existing combinations, effectively building\n    up the set of all possible combinations (including the empty list).\n    The order of combinations in the output matches the specific order\n    demonstrated in the provided assert statement.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: A list of elements for which to find combinations.\n\n    Returns:\n        A list of lists, where each inner list represents a unique combination\n        of elements from the input_list.\n    \"\"\"\n    all_combinations = [[]]  # Start with an empty list as the first combination\n\n    for element in input_list:\n        # Create new combinations by prepending the current element\n        # to all combinations generated so far.\n        new_combinations_with_current_element = []\n        for existing_combination in all_combinations:\n            new_combinations_with_current_element.append([element] + existing_combination)\n        \n        # Add these new combinations to the total list of combinations.\n        all_combinations.extend(new_combinations_with_current_element)\n            \n    return all_combinations\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "```python\ndef max_subarray_product(nums: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum product of a contiguous subarray within a given array.\n    This algorithm efficiently handles positive, negative, and zero integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nums:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = nums[0]\n    min_so_far = nums[0]\n    result = nums[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n        curr = nums[i]\n\n        # store the max_so_far because it will be changed\n        # when curr is negative, max_so_far becomes min_so_far * curr\n        # and min_so_far becomes max_so_far * curr\n        temp_max = max(curr, max_so_far * curr, min_so_far * curr)\n        temp_min = min(curr, max_so_far * curr, min_so_far * curr)\n\n        max_so_far = temp_max\n        min_so_far = temp_min\n\n        result = max(result, max_so_far)\n\n    return result\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Any, List\n\ndef combinations_list(items: List[Any]) -> List[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Generates all possible combinations of elements from a list, matching the specified output order.\"\"\"\n    all_combinations: List[List[Any]] = [[]]\n    for item in items:\n        # Create new combinations by adding the current item to the front of existing ones.\n        new_combos_for_this_item: List[List[Any]] = []\n        for combo in all_combinations:\n            new_combos_for_this_item.append([item] + combo)\n        all_combinations.extend(new_combos_for_this_item)\n    return all_combinations\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/465", "solution": "```python\ndef drop_empty(data: dict) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes key-value pairs from a dictionary where values are considered empty.\n    Empty values include None, empty strings, empty lists, empty tuples, and empty dictionaries.\n    \"\"\"\n    cleaned_data = {}\n    for key, value in data.items():\n        # Retain items whose values are not explicitly defined as empty.\n        if not (value is None or\n                value == \"\" or\n                value == [] or\n                value == () or\n                value == {}):\n            cleaned_data[key] = value\n    return cleaned_data\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "```python\ndef max_subarray_product(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum product of a contiguous subarray within a given array.\n    This function implements an O(N) dynamic programming approach.\n\n    Args:\n        arr: A list of integers.\n\n    Returns:\n        An integer representing the maximum product of any contiguous subarray.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input array is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input array cannot be empty.\")\n\n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    min_so_far = arr[0]\n    result = max_so_far\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        curr = arr[i]\n\n        # Calculate potential new max and min products ending at the current position.\n        # Store temp_max before updating min_so_far, as min_so_far might depend on the old max_so_far.\n        temp_max = max(curr, max_so_far * curr, min_so_far * curr)\n        min_so_far = min(curr, max_so_far * curr, min_so_far * curr)\n        max_so_far = temp_max\n\n        # Update the overall maximum product found so far.\n        result = max(max_so_far, result)\n\n    return result\n```\n"}
