{"task_id": "Mbpp/555", "solution": "```python\ndef difference(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the difference between the sum of cubes of the first 'n' natural numbers\n    and the sum of the first 'n' natural numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    # Calculate the sum of the first n natural numbers\n    sum_natural_numbers = n * (n + 1) // 2\n\n    # Calculate the sum of the cubes of the first n natural numbers\n    # which is the square of the sum of the first n natural numbers\n    sum_cubes_natural_numbers = sum_natural_numbers * sum_natural_numbers\n\n    # Calculate the difference\n    return sum_cubes_natural_numbers - sum_natural_numbers\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/554", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef Split(numbers: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Filters a list of integers, returning only the odd ones.\n    Performs type validation for the list and its elements.\n    Raises TypeError if the input is not a list or contains non-integer elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    \n    odd_numbers = []\n    for number in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(number, int):\n            raise TypeError(f\"All elements in the list must be integers, got {type(number).__name__}.\")\n        if number % 2 != 0:\n            odd_numbers.append(number)\n    return odd_numbers"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Odd_Pair(arr, n):\n    \"\"\"Counts pairs in arr whose bitwise XOR sum is odd.\n    An XOR sum is odd if one number in the pair is odd and the other is even.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    even_count = 0\n\n    for x in arr:\n        if x % 2 != 0:  # Check if x is odd\n            odd_count += 1\n        else:           # x is even\n            even_count += 1\n    \n    return odd_count * even_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/555", "solution": "```python\ndef difference(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the difference between the sum of cubes of the first n natural numbers and the sum of the first n natural numbers.\n    Returns 0 if n is less than or equal to 0, as per business rules.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _sum_natural_numbers(k: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the first k natural numbers.\"\"\"\n        if k <= 0:\n            return 0\n        return k * (k + 1) // 2\n\n    def _sum_cubes(k: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the cubes of the first k natural numbers.\"\"\"\n        if k <= 0:\n            return 0\n        sum_k = _sum_natural_numbers(k)\n        return sum_k ** 2\n\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n\n    sum_of_cubes_n = _sum_cubes(n)\n    sum_of_n = _sum_natural_numbers(n)\n\n    return sum_of_cubes_n - sum_of_n\n```"}
