{"task_id": "Mbpp/573", "solution": "```python\nimport math\nfrom typing import List, Union\n\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception raised for invalid input types or formats.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef unique_product(numbers_list: List[Union[int, float]]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the product of the unique numbers in a given list.\n\n    Args:\n        numbers_list: A list of numbers (integers or floats).\n\n    Returns:\n        The product of the unique numbers. Returns 1 if the list is empty.\n\n    Raises:\n        InvalidInputError: If the input is not a list or if the list contains non-numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers_list, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    if not numbers_list:\n        return 1\n\n    unique_numbers = set()\n    for item in numbers_list:\n        if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"List contains non-numeric element: {item}\")\n        unique_numbers.add(item)\n\n    if not unique_numbers: # This check handles cases where unique_numbers could theoretically become empty after filtering, though primary empty list case is handled above.\n        return 1\n\n    return math.prod(unique_numbers)\n```\n"}
