{"task_id": "Mbpp/594", "solution": "```python\ndef diff_even_odd(numbers: list[int | float]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the absolute difference between the first even and first odd integer\n    in a given list of numbers.\n\n    Args:\n        numbers: A list of integers and/or floats.\n\n    Returns:\n        The absolute difference between the first even and first odd integer.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If the input is not a list or contains non-numeric elements.\n        ValueError: If no even integer or no odd integer is found in the list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(numbers, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    first_even: int | None = None\n    first_odd: int | None = None\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if not isinstance(num, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(f\"List elements must be numbers, got {type(num)}\")\n\n        # Only consider integers for even/odd check\n        if isinstance(num, int):\n            if num % 2 == 0 and first_even is None:\n                first_even = num\n            elif num % 2 != 0 and first_odd is None:\n                first_odd = num\n\n        if first_even is not None and first_odd is not None:\n            break # Both found, no need to continue searching\n\n    if first_even is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"No even integer found in the list.\")\n    if first_odd is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"No odd integer found in the list.\")\n\n    return abs(first_even - first_odd)\n```"}
