{"task_id": "Mbpp/605", "solution": "```python\ndef prime_num(number: int) -> bool:\n    if number <= 1:\n        return False\n    if number <= 3:\n        return True\n    if number % 2 == 0 or number % 3 == 0:\n        return False\n    i = 5\n    while i * i <= number:\n        if number % i == 0 or number % (i + 2) == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 6\n    return True\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/605", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef prime_num(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given integer is a prime number.\n    Uses trial division up to the square root, optimized for even numbers.\"\"\"\n    if number <= 1:\n        return False\n    if number == 2:\n        return True\n    if number % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(number)) + 1, 2):\n        if number % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
