{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_Number(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using dynamic programming (Bell triangle).\n    This function computes Bell numbers for non-negative integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    bell = [[0 for _ in range(n + 1)] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    bell[0][0] = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        bell[i][0] = bell[i - 1][i - 1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            bell[i][j] = bell[i - 1][j - 1] + bell[i][j - 1]\n\n    return bell[n][0]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "```python\ndef bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number using the Bell triangle method.\n\n    Args:\n        n: A non-negative integer.\n\n    Returns:\n        The nth Bell number.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    # Initialize the Bell triangle (Aitken's array)\n    # We only need the current and previous row to compute the next\n    # For simplicity, we'll build the full triangle up to n\n    triangle = [[0 for _ in range(i + 1)] for i in range(n + 1)]\n\n    triangle[0][0] = 1\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # The first element of the current row is the last element of the previous row\n        triangle[i][0] = triangle[i-1][i-1] \n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # Each subsequent element is the sum of the element to its left\n            # and the element diagonally up-left from the previous row\n            triangle[i][j] = triangle[i][j-1] + triangle[i-1][j-1]\n        \n    return triangle[n][0]\n\n```"}
