{"task_id": "Mbpp/618", "solution": "```python\ndef div_list(list1: list[float | int], list2: list[float | int]) -> list[float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Divides elements of list1 by corresponding elements of list2 element-wise.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If the input lists have different lengths.\n        ZeroDivisionError: If any element in the second list (list2) is zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(list1) != len(list2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Lists must have the same length for element-wise division.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(list1)):\n        if list2[i] == 0:\n            raise ZeroDivisionError(f\"Division by zero encountered at index {i}.\")\n        result.append(float(list1[i]) / list2[i])\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/616", "solution": "```python\nclass TupleLengthMismatchError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for when tuple lengths do not match.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Input tuples must have the same length.\"):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\nclass DivisionByZeroError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for when a modulo by zero operation is attempted.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str = \"Cannot perform modulo by zero.\"):\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef tuple_modulo(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"Performs element-wise modulo on two tuples.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple1: The first tuple (dividend). Expected to contain numeric types.\n        tuple2: The second tuple (divisor). Expected to contain numeric types.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new tuple containing the results of the modulo operations.\n\n    Raises:\n        TupleLengthMismatchError: If the input tuples are not of the same length.\n        DivisionByZeroError: If any element in the second tuple (tuple2) is zero.\n        TypeError: If non-numeric types are encountered in the tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise TupleLengthMismatchError()\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        if tuple2[i] == 0:\n            raise DivisionByZeroError(f\"Cannot perform modulo by zero at index {i}.\")\n        result.append(tuple1[i] % tuple2[i])\n    return tuple(result)\n```\n"}
