{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "```python\ndef get_coordinates(coordinate_tuple: tuple[int, int]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates all coordinates in a 3x3 grid centered at the given coordinate, including itself.\n    Assumes the input coordinate_tuple is always a valid tuple of two integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coordinate_tuple\n    adjacent_coords = []\n    for dx in range(-1, 2):\n        for dy in range(-1, 2):\n            adjacent_coords.append([x + dx, y + dy])\n    return adjacent_coords\n```"}
