{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "```python\ndef wind_chill(velocity: float, temperature: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the wind chill index, rounded to the next integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _ceil(x: float) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Manually implements ceiling rounding for a float.\"\"\"\n        if x == int(x):\n            return int(x)\n        elif x > 0:\n            return int(x) + 1\n        else:\n            return int(x)\n\n\n    # For wind velocities below 4.8 km/h, the wind chill index is conventionally\n    # considered to be the actual air temperature.\n    if velocity < 4.8:\n        return _ceil(temperature)\n\n    # Wind Chill Formula (Environment Canada / US NWS standard for Celsius and km/h)\n    # WC = 13.12 + 0.6215*T - 11.37*V^0.16 + 0.3965*T*V^0.16\n    wind_chill_float = (\n        13.12\n        + (0.6215 * temperature)\n        - (11.37 * (velocity**0.16))\n        + (0.3965 * temperature * (velocity**0.16))\n    )\n    return _ceil(wind_chill_float)\n```"}
