{"task_id": "Mbpp/638", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\n# NWS Wind Chill Formula Constants\nNWS_WC_CONST_A = 35.74\nNWS_WC_CONST_B = 0.6215\nNWS_WC_CONST_C = 35.75\nNWS_WC_CONST_D = 0.4275\n\n# Unit Conversion Factors\nKMH_TO_MPH_FACTOR = 1.60934  # 1 mile = 1.60934 km\nCELSIUS_TO_FAHRENHEIT_FACTOR = 1.8  # Equivalent to 9/5\nFAHRENHEIT_OFFSET = 32.0\n\n\ndef wind_chill(velocity: float, temperature: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the wind chill index given wind velocity in km/h and temperature in Celsius.\n    The result is rounded down to the nearest integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert Celsius temperature to Fahrenheit\n    temp_f = temperature * CELSIUS_TO_FAHRENHEIT_FACTOR + FAHRENHEIT_OFFSET\n\n    # Convert wind velocity from km/h to mph\n    vel_mph = velocity / KMH_TO_MPH_FACTOR\n\n    # If wind speed is 3 mph or less, wind chill is equal to air temperature.\n    if vel_mph <= 3.0:\n        wind_chill_f = temp_f\n    else:\n        # Apply the NWS Wind Chill Formula (Fahrenheit, mph)\n        wind_chill_f = (NWS_WC_CONST_A +\n                        NWS_WC_CONST_B * temp_f -\n                        NWS_WC_CONST_C * (vel_mph ** 0.16) +\n                        NWS_WC_CONST_D * temp_f * (vel_mph ** 0.16))\n\n    # Convert the calculated wind chill index from Fahrenheit back to Celsius\n    wind_chill_c = (wind_chill_f - FAHRENHEIT_OFFSET) / CELSIUS_TO_FAHRENHEIT_FACTOR\n\n    # Round the wind chill index by truncating the decimal part (floor)\n    return math.floor(wind_chill_c)\n```\n"}
