{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "```python\ndef reverse_Array_Upto_K(arr: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the elements of the input list 'arr' from index 0 up to (but not including) index 'k' in-place.\n    The function modifies and returns the input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    left = 0\n    right = k - 1\n\n    while left < right:\n        arr[left], arr[right] = arr[right], arr[left]\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n    return arr\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "```python\ndef reverse_Array_Upto_K(arr, k):\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses the first `k` elements of the input `arr` in-place.\n    The modified `arr` is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    left, right = 0, k - 1\n    while left < right:\n        arr[left], arr[right] = arr[right], arr[left]\n        left += 1\n        right -= 1\n    return arr\n```"}
