{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with 'n' digits.\n    Assumes 'n' is a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    lower_bound = 10**(n - 1)\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        triangular_number = k * (k + 1) // 2\n        if triangular_number >= lower_bound:\n            return k\n        k += 1\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "```python\ndef find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with `n` digits.\n    It iterates to find the first triangular number that is greater than or equal to 10^(n-1).\n    \"\"\"\n    lower_bound = 10**(n - 1)\n\n    k = 1\n    triangular_number = 1\n\n    while triangular_number < lower_bound:\n        k += 1\n        triangular_number = k * (k + 1) // 2\n    \n    return k\n```"}
