{"task_id": "Mbpp/742", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef area_tetrahedron(side_length: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the total surface area of a regular tetrahedron.\n\n    Args:\n        side_length: The length of one side of the tetrahedron. Must be a non-negative float.\n\n    Returns:\n        The total surface area as a float.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If side_length is negative.\n        TypeError: If side_length is not a numeric type.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(side_length, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"side_length must be a numeric type.\")\n    if side_length < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"side_length cannot be negative.\")\n\n    # Formula for the total surface area of a regular tetrahedron: Area = sqrt(3) * a^2\n    area = math.sqrt(3) * (side_length ** 2)\n    return area\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "```python\ndef rotate_right(data: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a list by n positions to the right, returning a new list.\n    Handles empty lists, negative n (left rotation), and n values beyond list length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        return []\n\n    length = len(data)\n    \n    # Normalize the rotation amount 'n'.\n    # Convert negative 'n' (left rotation) into an equivalent positive right rotation.\n    if n < 0:\n        n = length + (n % length)\n    \n    # Ensure 'n' is within the valid range [0, length-1] using modulo arithmetic.\n    normalized_n = n % length\n    \n    # Perform the rotation using Python's list slicing for efficiency.\n    return data[-normalized_n:] + data[:-normalized_n]\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "```python\ndef rotate_right(data_list, rotation_count):\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    A new list is returned, leaving the original list unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data_list:\n        return []\n\n    n = len(data_list)\n    effective_rotation = rotation_count % n\n\n    if effective_rotation == 0:\n        return list(data_list)\n\n    rotated_list = data_list[n - effective_rotation:] + data_list[:n - effective_rotation]\n    return rotated_list\n```"}
