{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_divisible_by_all_digits(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is divisible by all its non-zero digits.\n    This function skips the digit 0 during divisibility checks.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return False\n\n    temp_num = number\n    while temp_num > 0:\n        digit = temp_num % 10\n        if digit == 0:\n            temp_num //= 10\n            continue\n        if number % digit != 0:\n            return False\n        temp_num //= 10\n    return True\n\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within an inclusive range that are divisible by all their non-zero digits.\n    It iterates through each number and uses a helper to check the condition.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    for number in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        if _is_divisible_by_all_digits(number):\n            results.append(number)\n    return results\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "```python\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum, endnum):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers in a range where each is divisible by all its non-zero digits.\n    Numbers containing the digit zero are excluded from the results.\n    \"\"\"\n    results = []\n    for number in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        str_num = str(number)\n        is_candidate = True\n        \n        for char_digit in str_num:\n            digit = int(char_digit)\n            if digit == 0:\n                is_candidate = False  # Number contains zero, thus disqualified.\n                break\n            if number % digit != 0:\n                is_candidate = False  # Not divisible by one of its digits.\n                break\n        \n        if is_candidate:\n            results.append(number)\n            \n    return results\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/748", "solution": "```python\ndef capital_words_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Inserts spaces before capitalized words in a string.\n    Returns the modified string with spaces inserted.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    result_chars = []\n    for i, char in enumerate(input_string):\n        if i > 0 and char.isupper() and input_string[i-1] != ' ':\n            result_chars.append(' ')\n        result_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/748", "solution": "```python\ndef capital_words_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Inserts spaces before words starting with capital letters, except for the very first character.\n    Handles consecutive uppercase letters appropriately (e.g., \"HTTPRequest\" -> \"HTTP Request\").\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    result_chars = [input_string[0]]\n    for i in range(1, len(input_string)):\n        char = input_string[i]\n        prev_char = input_string[i - 1]\n\n        should_add_space = False\n        # Insert a space if the current character is uppercase\n        if char.isupper():\n            # Condition 1: Previous character was not uppercase (e.g., \"helloWorld\")\n            if not prev_char.isupper():\n                should_add_space = True\n            # Condition 2: Previous character was uppercase, but the next character is lowercase\n            # This handles cases like \"HTTPRequest\" where a space is needed before 'R' but not between 'H','T','T','P'.\n            elif i + 1 < len(input_string) and input_string[i + 1].islower():\n                should_add_space = True\n        \n        if should_add_space:\n            result_chars.append(' ')\n        result_chars.append(char)\n        \n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
