{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "```python\ndef find_min_diff(arr: tuple, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in a given array.\n\n    Args:\n        arr (tuple): The input array of numeric elements.\n        n (int): The length of the input array.\n\n    Returns:\n        int: The minimum absolute difference.\n\n    Raises:\n        TypeError: If arr is not a tuple or n is not an integer.\n        ValueError: If n does not match len(arr) or if n < 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    MIN_ARRAY_LENGTH = 2\n\n    if not isinstance(arr, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'arr' must be a tuple.\")\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n != len(arr):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Input 'n' ({n}) must match the actual length of 'arr' ({len(arr)}).\")\n    if n < MIN_ARRAY_LENGTH:\n        raise ValueError(f\"Input array must contain at least {MIN_ARRAY_LENGTH} elements to find a difference.\")\n\n    # Convert tuple to list for sorting, as tuples are immutable\n    temp_list = list(arr)\n    temp_list.sort()\n\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        diff = abs(temp_list[i+1] - temp_list[i])\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n            \n    return int(min_diff)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "```python\ndef find_min_diff(arr, length):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum absolute difference between any two elements in the given array.\n    The 'length' parameter is ignored as len(arr) is used for array sizing.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_arr = sorted(arr)\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    for i in range(len(sorted_arr) - 1):\n        diff = abs(sorted_arr[i+1] - sorted_arr[i])\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n            \n    return int(min_diff)\n```"}
