{"task_id": "Mbpp/767", "solution": "```python\nimport collections\n\ndef get_pairs_count(numbers: list, sum: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts pairs in a list that sum up to a target value.\n    This implementation efficiently counts unique pairs of indices using a hash map.\n    \"\"\"\n    pair_count = 0\n    freq_map = collections.defaultdict(int)\n\n    for number in numbers:\n        complement = sum - number\n        if complement in freq_map:\n            pair_count += freq_map[complement]\n        freq_map[number] += 1\n    return pair_count\n```"}
