{"task_id": "Mbpp/771", "solution": "```python\ndef check_expression(expression: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given string expression has balanced delimiters (parentheses, brackets, braces).\n    Uses a stack to ensure correct LIFO order matching.\n    \"\"\"\n    OPENING_DELIMITERS: str = \"({[\"\n    CLOSING_DELIMITERS: str = \")}]\"\n    DELIMITER_MAP: dict[str, str] = {\n        \"(\": \")\",\n        \"{\": \"}\",\n        \"[\": \"]\",\n    }\n\n    stack: list[str] = []\n\n    for char in expression:\n        if char in OPENING_DELIMITERS:\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char in CLOSING_DELIMITERS:\n            if not stack:\n                return False\n            \n            last_opening = stack.pop()\n            # We need to map the opening delimiter to its closing counterpart\n            # and then compare with the current closing character.\n            # Example: if last_opening is '(', DELIMITER_MAP['('] should be ')'\n            # If the current char ')' matches, then it's balanced.\n            if DELIMITER_MAP.get(last_opening) != char:\n                return False\n        \n    return not stack\n```"}
