{"task_id": "Mbpp/780", "solution": "```python\nimport itertools\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Union\n\ndef find_combinations(input_list: List[Tuple[Union[int, float], Union[int, float]]]) -> List[Tuple[Union[int, float], Union[int, float]]]:\n    \"\"\"Finds all unique combinations of two distinct 2-element tuples from input_list.\n    Returns a new list containing the element-wise sum for each pair.\"\"\"\n    if len(input_list) < 2:\n        return []\n\n    result_combinations: List[Tuple[Union[int, float], Union[int, float]]] = []\n    for tuple_a, tuple_b in itertools.combinations(input_list, 2):\n        sum_x = tuple_a[0] + tuple_b[0]\n        sum_y = tuple_a[1] + tuple_b[1]\n        result_combinations.append((sum_x, sum_y))\n\n    return result_combinations\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/780", "solution": "```python\nfrom itertools import combinations\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Any, Union\n\ndef find_combinations(tuple_list: List[Tuple[Any, ...]]) -> List[Tuple[Union[int, float], Union[int, float]]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds combinations of sums by pairing elements from input tuples.\n    Assumes input tuples each contain at least two numerical elements for pairing.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_sums = []\n    for t1, t2 in combinations(tuple_list, 2):\n        sum1 = t1[0] + t2[0]\n        sum2 = t1[1] + t2[1]\n        result_sums.append((sum1, sum2))\n    return result_sums\n```"}
