{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "```python\ndef last(arr: list, x: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array.\n    Returns the index of the last occurrence of x, or -1 if not present.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Try to find further occurrences on the right\n        elif arr[mid] < x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return result\n```"}
