{"task_id": "Mbpp/809", "solution": "```python\ndef check_smaller(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if each element of the second tuple is strictly smaller than its corresponding element in the first tuple.\n    Assumes inputs are valid tuples of numbers with the same length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple1, tuple) or not isinstance(tuple2, tuple):\n        raise ValueError(\"Both inputs must be tuples.\")\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        e1 = tuple1[i]\n        e2 = tuple2[i]\n        if not isinstance(e1, (int, float)) or not isinstance(e2, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(\"Tuple elements must be numbers.\")\n        if not (e2 < e1):\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
